        <ArticleTitle>Interleukin-6 and autoimmunity: a review of the pathogenic role of IL-6 in rheumatoid arthritis.</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND">Interleukin-6 (IL-6) is a pleiotropic cytokine with a central role in rheumatoid arthritis.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="FINDINGS">IL-6 activates JAK/STAT3 signalling in synovial tissue, promotes Th17 differentiation and supports B-cell autoantibody production. IL-6 receptor blockade reduces C-reactive protein and improves tender joint counts in patients with rheumatoid arthritis.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
