        <ArticleTitle>Randomised controlled trial of interleukin-6 receptor blockade in active rheumatoid arthritis.</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>In this randomised controlled trial, interleukin-6 receptor blockade improved American College of Rheumatology response rates and reduced disease activity scores in patients with active rheumatoid arthritis. Serious infection rates were modestly increased.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
